  "description": "XALZER crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C82 H155 Ce10 N5 Na1 O48. From the CIF bond table, Ce1 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce2 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce3 (Ce) has 9 O neighbors; Ce4 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce5 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce6 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce7 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce8 (Ce) has 8 O neighbors; Ce9 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors; Ce10 (Ce) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 24 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.603-4.142 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 91.00-136.28°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C82H155Ce10N5NaO48. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 1 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
